---
/**
 * website/src/components/ZoomLevels.astro — the four levels, drawn from the owner's boards
 * (the brief of 2026-10-22; D237, D244, D245, D247, D248/D249).
 *
 * **What this replaces.** Part 4 (#852) drew the four levels as the site's own diagrams, and the
 * owner's reading of 2026-10-22 is that they were terrible. The four boards in
 * `website/design-ref/zoom-levels/level1.dc.html` … `level4.dc.html` — 1280x720, drawn in Claude
 * Design and approved by the owner — are the source of truth, and this component is those boards
 * redrawn as the site's inline SVG: the same boxes, the same labels word for word, the same
 * arrows including the bent and double-headed ones, the same colours, and the boards' own
 * explanatory paragraph under each drawing.
 *
 * **The shapes are shared, and that is the point** (D244). One `<defs>`, in the zero-size
 * `<svg class="zoom-defs">` under the heading, holds one `<symbol>` per entity the boards draw —
 * the job tile, the container a job is, the laptop, the cloud project, the whole project, the
 * console card, the Fugaro card, the draft pull request, the orchestrator pill, the developer
 * card and the person in it, the phone app and the planned card. Every level draws an entity
 * **only** through `<use href="#zoom-…">`, so a job tile is the same tile in all four levels, and
 * the first edit that redraws one level's copy of it is what `website/test/how-it-works.mjs`
 * refuses. The symbols are referenced across `<svg>` elements within this one document, which is
 * how a sprite sheet works: the ids are document-wide, the `<defs>` is written once, and the four
 * drawings stay four drawings a browser lays out separately.
 *
 * A symbol is stretched to the box the board draws it in (`preserveAspectRatio="none"`), which is
 * what makes one job tile serve a 168x76 tile and a 200x60 row, and every symbol's stroke is
 * `vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"`, so a 2 px board border is 2 units at every size rather
 * than 0.3 units inside the one big box and 14 units inside a tile. Where a board's own corner
 * radius would scale into a wobble — the one big job box, the cloud box, the project box — the
 * symbol carries its own viewBox at the size the board draws it, so the radius is the board's.
 *
 * **The words are the boards' own.** Every label is drawn as real SVG `<text>` in the site's font
 * stack, and `holdZoomBoards` holds every one of them to the board file it was drawn from at
 * build time (Global Constraint 6, `src/lib/zoom-boards.mjs`): a word the component changed stops
 * the build naming the file. `website/test/how-it-works.mjs` reads the same boards the other way
 * round — every string a board prints is a `<text>` of its level — so a label the drawing dropped
 * is a failure there rather than a silence here. A card's text wraps onto the lines its own width
 * holds, which is what the boards' own browser rendering does with the same text at the same
 * size; the wrapped pieces are consecutive, so the board's line is still the level's words.
 *
 * **One `<nav>` of markers, and no script** (D245). Four anchors, `#level-1` … `#level-4`, each
 * with an accessible name, mirroring the console slider's dots: the linkcheck gate resolves them,
 * a no-JS reader can use them, and Part 5 reuses the same ids rather than adding a second set.
 * Every level is a still: nothing here moves, nothing here is measured by a script, and the
 * pinned scroll-driven zoom between the four is Part 5 and not this component.
 *
 * **A level is a picture with a name, so it is one `role="img"`.** The four levels are not lists
 * of labelled parts any more: the board is one drawing, its own headline and paragraph are part
 * of it, and a reader who cannot see it is given the board's title and its subtitle through
 * `<title>`/`<desc>` rather than forty loose labels read out in the order the markup happens to
 * have. The `<figcaption>` names the figure in the document flow, which is where a reader meets
 * it.
 *
 * **The words stay legible when the drawing shrinks.** At the page's widest column the 1280-unit
 * board is drawn at 1152 units, so a label the board sets at 11 px renders at 9.9 px — and at a
 * phone's 390 px column it would render at 3.4 px, which is not text at all. So below the phone
 * breakpoint the figure keeps a floor (`min-width`) and scrolls sideways inside its own box
 * rather than shrinking below it, and the labels that would still fall under 10 px rendered — the
 * board's 11, 12 and 13 px eyebrows and notes — are drawn inside `<g class="zoom-fine">`, which
 * the same breakpoint hides. Nothing is ever shrunk below the floor, and what a phone reader
 * loses is the small print, not the drawing: the shapes, the arrows and the colours are all
 * still there, and the level's title, subtitle, card labels and paragraph are all still read.
 * `website/test/how-it-works.mjs` reads both halves against the floor this file's stylesheet
 * declares — every label the phone keeps at 10 px or more, and every label it drops at less —
 * so a label of a board's small print written outside the group is refused rather than shipped
 * at 9 px.
 *
 * **Nothing is fetched, nothing is a picture file, no colour is a literal in the markup and no
 * font is load-bearing.** The boards' colours are named CSS variables on the section (`--zoom-*`)
 * — the boards are drawn on the palette's own ground (`--ground`, the one board colour that is
 * exactly a site token) with a set of colours the site does not otherwise use — and the rules
 * that paint the generated shapes carry `:global()` because the markup arrives through
 * `set:html`, which Astro's scope attribute never reaches (the defect of 2026-10-21).
 */
import { BOARDS, holdZoomBoards } from '../lib/zoom-boards.mjs'

/** The drawing's own coordinates: every board is 1280x720, and the viewBox is the board's. */
const W = 1280
const H = 720

/** The per-character width a label is laid out with, as a fraction of its size: the boards set
 *  Inter, whose lowercase runs a little over half an em, and a wrapped line that is a few units
 *  wider than this estimate is a line the card has room for. */
const CHAR = 0.55

/**
 * The size a board's small print is set at, and below which a label is drawn inside the
 * `<g class="zoom-fine">` the phone hides: the drawing keeps a floor of 920 units on a phone
 * (`min-width`, see the styles), so a label the boards set at 14 px renders at 10.06 px there and
 * a label they set at 13 px renders at 9.34 px — which is not text. Every label under this size
 * is the small print the phone loses, and a label of exactly this size is the smallest one it
 * keeps. `website/test/how-it-works.mjs` holds both halves against the floor the stylesheet
 * declares, so a label of a board's small print drawn outside the group is refused rather than
 * shipped at 9 px.
 */
const SMALL_PRINT = 14

const esc = (text) =>
  String(text).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;')

const width = (text, size) => String(text).length * CHAR * size

/** The lines a column holds, wrapped on the spaces: a card is as wide as the board draws it, and
 *  the board's own rendering wraps the same text at the same size the same way. */
function wrap(text, room, size) {
  const lines = []
  let line = ''
  for (const word of String(text).split(' ')) {
    const next = line === '' ? word : `${line} ${word}`
    if (line !== '' && width(next, size) > room) {
      lines.push(line)
      line = word
    } else {
      line = next
    }
  }
  if (line !== '') lines.push(line)
  return lines
}

/** One entity, drawn from the one `<defs>`: a level never draws a shape of its own (D244). */
const entity = (id, x, y, w, h) => `<use class="zoom-entity" href="#${id}" x="${x}" y="${y}" width="${w}" height="${h}" />`

/** One line of a level's words, as real text: the board's own string, at the board's own size. */
function label(words, text, x, y, opts = {}) {
  const classes = ['zoom-word', opts.ink ?? 'zoom-ink']
  if (opts.upper === true) classes.push('zoom-upper')
  if (opts.display === true) classes.push('zoom-display')
  const attrs = [
    `class="${classes.join(' ')}"`,
    `x="${x}"`,
    `y="${y}"`,
    `font-size="${opts.size}"`,
    opts.anchor === undefined ? '' : `text-anchor="${opts.anchor}"`,
    opts.weight === undefined ? '' : `font-weight="${opts.weight}"`,
  ].filter((part) => part !== '')
  words.push(text)
  return `<text ${attrs.join(' ')}>${esc(text)}</text>`
}

/**
 * One card of a board: the entity it is drawn from, the person in it when the board draws one,
 * and the card's words, centred on the card's own middle the way the board's flex box centres
 * them. A line the card's width cannot hold is wrapped, and the lines are stepped by the board's
 * own line-height.
 */
function card(words, opts) {
  const { id, x, y, w, h, lines, icon = null, step = 20, lead = 14 } = opts
  const drawn = lines.flatMap((line) => wrap(line.text, w - 12, line.size).map((text) => ({ ...line, text })))
  const iconRoom = icon === null ? 0 : 32
  const top = y + h / 2 - (iconRoom + drawn.length * step) / 2
  const cx = x + w / 2
  const parts = [entity(id, x, y, w, h)]
  if (icon !== null) parts.push(entity(icon, cx - 14, top, 28, 28))
  const small = []
  for (const [index, line] of drawn.entries()) {
    const markup = label(words, line.text, cx, top + iconRoom + index * step + lead, {
      size: line.size,
      weight: line.weight,
      anchor: 'middle',
      ink: line.ink,
    })
    // A line of the board's small print goes inside the group the phone hides, wherever it is
    // drawn: the card's own shape and its title stay, and the note under them goes with the
    // other small print (see `SMALL_PRINT`).
    if (line.size < SMALL_PRINT) small.push(markup)
    else parts.push(markup)
  }
  if (small.length > 0) parts.push(`<g class="zoom-fine">${small.join('')}</g>`)
  return `<g class="zoom-card">${parts.join('')}</g>`
}

/** The board's explanatory paragraph, wrapped to the board's own column and stepped by its
 *  line-height: the last thing a board says, and the plainest sentence of the four levels. */
function paragraph(words, text, x, y, room) {
  return wrap(text, room, 14)
    .map((line, index) => label(words, line, x, y + index * 22, { size: 14, ink: 'zoom-ink-muted' }))
    .join('')
}

/** One arrow of a board, as a stroked path: the board's own geometry, tip on the endpoint. */
function arrow(d, tone, opts = {}) {
  const parts = [`class="zoom-arrow zoom-arrow-${tone}"`, `d="${d}"`]
  if (opts.dashed === true) parts.push('stroke-dasharray="6 6"')
  if (opts.start === true) parts.push(`marker-start="url(#zoom-head-${tone})"`)
  if (opts.end !== false) parts.push(`marker-end="url(#zoom-head-${tone})"`)
  return `<path ${parts.join(' ')} />`
}

/**
 * The one `<defs>`: an arrowhead per tone, and a `<symbol>` per entity the boards draw. Every
 * `<rect>` is inset by half its stroke so the border is not clipped, and carries
 * `vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"` so the width is the board's at every size the symbol is
 * stretched to.
 */
const head = (tone) =>
  `<marker id="zoom-head-${tone}" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="8" refY="4" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path class="zoom-head zoom-head-${tone}" d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" /></marker>`

const box = (stroke, fill, inset, rx, w, h) =>
  `<rect class="zoom-shape ${fill} ${stroke}" x="${inset}" y="${inset}" width="${w - 2 * inset}" height="${h - 2 * inset}" rx="${rx}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />`

const person = (id, cls) =>
  `<symbol id="${id}" viewBox="0 0 28 28" preserveAspectRatio="none"><circle class="${cls}" cx="14" cy="9" r="5" /><path class="${cls}" d="M4 25 C4 18 9 15 14 15 C19 15 24 18 24 25" /></symbol>`

const SYMBOLS = [
  head('grey'),
  head('accent'),
  head('green'),
  head('planned'),
  // The job: the boards draw it as a 2 px orange rounded rectangle at four sizes, and the tile's
  // own viewBox is the size the boards draw the tile at.
  `<symbol id="zoom-job" viewBox="0 0 168 76" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-accent', 'zoom-fill-card', 1, 14, 168, 76)}</symbol>`,
  // The one big box a level-1 job is, at the size the board draws it: a 14-unit corner radius
  // stretched onto a 1152x440 box would be a 40-unit corner, which is not the board's box.
  `<symbol id="zoom-box" viewBox="0 0 1152 440" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-accent', 'zoom-fill-panel', 1, 20, 1152, 440)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-cloud" viewBox="0 0 280 330" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-accent', 'zoom-fill-panel', 1, 20, 280, 330)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-laptop" viewBox="0 0 520 330" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-edge', 'zoom-fill-panel', 0.5, 20, 520, 330)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-project" viewBox="0 0 640 420" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-project', 'zoom-fill-panel', 1, 24, 640, 420)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-loop" viewBox="0 0 208 324" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-loop', 'zoom-fill-loop', 0.5, 14, 208, 324)}</symbol>`,
  // The card, and the two cards that are a card with another border: the boards draw the console,
  // the Firebase project and the plain cards with the same shape.
  `<symbol id="zoom-card" viewBox="0 0 176 84" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-edge', 'zoom-fill-card', 0.5, 12, 176, 84)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-card-accent" viewBox="0 0 176 84" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-accent-thin', 'zoom-fill-card', 0.5, 12, 176, 84)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-card-planned" viewBox="0 0 176 84" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-planned', 'zoom-fill-panel', 0.5, 12, 176, 84)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-phone" viewBox="0 0 160 80" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-planned', 'zoom-fill-panel', 0.5, 16, 160, 80)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-firebase" viewBox="0 0 240 80" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-edge', 'zoom-fill-card', 0.5, 12, 240, 80)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-draft-pr" viewBox="0 0 176 96" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-green', 'zoom-fill-green', 0.5, 12, 176, 96)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-orchestrator" viewBox="0 0 200 92" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-blue', 'zoom-fill-card', 0.5, 50, 200, 92)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-developer" viewBox="0 0 128 120" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-blue', 'zoom-fill-card', 0.5, 12, 128, 120)}</symbol>`,
  `<symbol id="zoom-developer-planned" viewBox="0 0 112 120" preserveAspectRatio="none">${box('zoom-line-planned', 'zoom-fill-panel', 0.5, 12, 112, 120)}</symbol>`,
  person('zoom-person', 'zoom-person'),
  person('zoom-person-planned', 'zoom-person-planned'),
].join('')

/** One level: its board's title, the board's own subtitle, and the drawing. */
function level(id, draw) {
  const board = BOARDS.find((entry) => entry.id === id)
  const words = []
  const { body, fine, title, subtitle } = draw(words)
  return {
    id,
    name: board.name,
    title,
    subtitle,
    words,
    markup: [
      `<title id="${id}-title">${esc(title)}</title>`,
      `<desc>${esc(subtitle)}</desc>`,
      body.join(''),
      fine.length === 0 ? '' : `<g class="zoom-fine">${fine.join('')}</g>`,
    ].join(''),
  }
}

/** Level 1 — inside one job: one Cloud Run job, the first-line loop and the bounce back. */
function level1() {
  return level('level-1', (words) => {
    const title = 'Inside one job'
    const subtitle = 'Level 1 of 4. One run is one ephemeral cloud job.'
    const fine = [
      label(words, 'One Cloud Run job, one per run', 88, 176, { size: 12, ink: 'zoom-ink-accent', weight: 600, upper: true }),
      label(words, 'First line', 408, 253, { size: 11, ink: 'zoom-ink-muted', weight: 600, upper: true }),
      label(words, 'one bounce back', 640, 197, { size: 13, ink: 'zoom-ink-accent', anchor: 'middle' }),
    ]
    const body = [
      entity('zoom-box', 64, 150, 1152, 440),
      entity('zoom-loop', 392, 238, 208, 324),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-card', x: 120, y: 358, w: 176, h: 84, lines: [{ text: 'Checks', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'compile, tests', size: 14 }] }),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-card', x: 408, y: 270, w: 176, h: 84, lines: [{ text: 'Coder', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'writes the change', size: 14 }] }),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-card', x: 408, y: 446, w: 176, h: 84, lines: [{ text: 'Reviewer', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'first-line review', size: 14 }] }),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-card-accent', x: 696, y: 358, w: 176, h: 84, lines: [{ text: 'Senior review', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'a stronger model', size: 14 }] }),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-draft-pr', x: 984, y: 352, w: 176, h: 96, lines: [{ text: 'Draft PR', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'ready only on senior ship', size: 14 }, { text: 'and passing tests', size: 14 }] }),
      arrow('M296 400 H392', 'grey'),
      arrow('M467 354 V446', 'grey'),
      arrow('M525 446 V354', 'grey'),
      arrow('M600 400 H696', 'grey'),
      arrow('M872 400 H984', 'grey'),
      arrow('M496 214 H784', 'accent', { dashed: true, end: false }),
      arrow('M784 214 V358', 'accent', { dashed: true, end: false }),
      arrow('M496 214 V238', 'accent'),
      label(words, title, 64, 90, { size: 32, weight: 700, display: true }),
      label(words, subtitle, 64, 121, { size: 16, ink: 'zoom-ink-muted' }),
      paragraph(
        words,
        'Checks run first when the recipe asks for them. The coder and the first-line reviewer go round for as many rounds as the recipe allows. Then the senior review judges the result; if it rejects, the work bounces back once, then the run fails. A draft pull request becomes ready only when the senior review ships it and the tests pass on the final commit.',
        64,
        640,
        1152,
      ),
    ]
    return { body, fine, title, subtitle }
  })
}

/** Level 2 — one orchestrator, many jobs: the fan-out, and the draft pull requests coming back. */
function level2() {
  return level('level-2', (words) => {
    const title = 'One orchestrator, many jobs'
    const subtitle = 'Level 2 of 4. Each job is the tile from level 1.'
    const fine = [label(words, 'fugaro run', 348, 343, { size: 13, ink: 'zoom-ink-muted', anchor: 'middle' })]
    const body = [
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-orchestrator', x: 96, y: 314, w: 200, h: 92, lines: [{ text: 'Orchestrator', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'an agent on the', size: 14 }, { text: "developer's machine", size: 14 }] }),
      card(words, { id: 'zoom-card', x: 400, y: 314, w: 200, h: 92, lines: [{ text: 'Fugaro', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'checks the budget,', size: 14 }, { text: 'then launches runs', size: 14 }] }),
      ...[190, 322, 454].flatMap((top) => [
        card(words, { id: 'zoom-job', x: 800, y: top, w: 168, h: 76, lines: [{ text: 'Job', size: 16, weight: 700 }, { text: 'one run', size: 14 }] }),
        card(words, { id: 'zoom-draft-pr', x: 1040, y: top, w: 144, h: 76, lines: [{ text: 'Draft PR', size: 16, weight: 700 }] }),
      ]),
      arrow('M296 360 H400', 'grey'),
      arrow('M600 360 H700', 'grey', { end: false }),
      arrow('M700 228 V492', 'grey', { end: false }),
      arrow('M700 228 H800', 'grey'),
      arrow('M700 360 H800', 'grey'),
      arrow('M700 492 H800', 'grey'),
      ...['228', '360', '492'].map((y) => arrow(`M968 ${y} H1040`, 'green')),
      label(words, title, 64, 90, { size: 32, weight: 700, display: true }),
      label(words, subtitle, 64, 121, { size: 16, ink: 'zoom-ink-muted' }),
      paragraph(
        words,
        'The orchestrator asks Fugaro for several runs at once. Fugaro takes a lease on the budget for each and launches the jobs in parallel; a launch the caps would exceed is refused. Every draft pull request flows back to the orchestrator.',
        64,
        640,
        1152,
      ),
    ]
    return { body, fine, title, subtitle }
  })
}

/** Level 3 — the developer's view: the laptop on the left, the cloud project on the right. */
function level3() {
